606946a11f00ea","ff9a03912482424b","ffcd83bb62d58d2c"],"groups":["3642450da2847844","296609ebf23dcffb","9d79a0dc87ab4a66","d5488eb6186423ad","05a5da09f2d455ca","e1c5cd8fdf7700a5","347372086fc95f48","12aa4ec975119775","e18a720f10a1179b","9269c558b87661c0","ba3024388ac88076","1c0841d71fc3e776"],"findings":"## Review of snapshot d968c40 (untrusted-input audit)\n\nI ran `test/untrusted.test.ts` (12/12 pass, including the two browser tests) and `tsc` (clean). I made no changes to the repo; scratch work is under `scratch/`. Most group annotations hold up. The mismatches below are the exceptions.\n\n### 1. Mismatches\n\n- **audit-todo: unrelated TODO item deleted, not reported.** The snapshot removes \"Bump the git-gloss dependency in git-gud (… cannot read format-4 glosses …)\" from the Release section. It is not part of the audit, is not marked done, and the audit group says it only drops done items. Anyone reading the TODO loses a cross-repo release blocker. **Verified:** `git show HEAD~1:TODO.md` has it at line 17, and the working `TODO.md` does not.\n- **audit-todo: wrong exit code recorded.** The TODO says the refspec glob makes every fetch \"exit 1\". I reproduced it: a remote that deletes `refs/notes/gloss/x` and then creates `refs/notes/gloss` makes `git fetch` fail with \"cannot lock ref … exists; cannot create\", exit **128**. The bug is real and correctly left unfixed; only the code is wrong. **Verified.**\n- **proto-free-maps: the same prototype bug remains in another place.** `src/reviews.ts:342` does `WORDS[s.stage] ?? WORDS.default`, and `WORDS` is a plain object. A review whose stage is `constructor` or `__proto__` gets an inherited value. I called `statusPhrase` directly and got `constructor: undefined (a, 2026-01-01)` and `__proto__: undefined (…)`. The author fixed this class in `client.js` but not here, and the audit does not list it. **Verified.** Fix: `Object.hasOwn(WORDS, s.stage)` or a `Map`.\n\n### 2. Misgraded necessity\n\n- **note-limits [required]:** this group bundles three things. The group-count cap, the risk cap and the claim-factor refusal were all reproduced. The `alternatives.max(MAX_ITEMS)` and `attention.reasons.max(MAX_ITEMS)` caps were not: the test covers groups and risks only. Under the task's own rule (\"fix only what was reproduced\") those two caps are **speculative** and should be split out or dropped. **Read.**\n- **note-limits, claim factor:** a legitimate gloss in which several groups share a hunk, and whose total claims exceed 5× the commit's changed lines, is now refused outright. This is a judgement call, not a reproduced need, and the rejection hits `show` and `html` for the whole range. The author already lists this as a risk. **Read.**\n- **markdown-bound [required]:** accurate. The test passes with hostile input of roughly 210 KB in total and asserts under 3 s. Note that the \"450 KB\" case is now moot because the review cap is 256 KiB, and the 256 KiB worst case was not timed. **Read** for the 256 KiB case.\n- **review-cap, terminal-clean, ary-url-crash, sync-tracking:** grades look right, and I confirmed the `//[` fix and the sync non-commit check are in the code.\n\n### 3. Removal candidates\n\n- The `alternatives` and `attention.reasons` caps (see above). Removing them has negligible impact on the reproduced fixes.\n\n### 4. Simplifications\n\n- The proto fix belongs in one place: a `Map` (or `Object.hasOwn`) in `reviews.ts` plus the existing `Object.create(null)` maps would cover the remaining lookups. Small change.\n\n### 5. Missing risks\n\n- **review-cap: silent verdict change.** A review line over 256 KiB is dropped with only a stderr warning. If it was the only `issues` verdict for a stage, the stage can show as clean (from an earlier review) or as merely \"reviewed\" in `show`, and the html page shows no warning. Fail-open for the verdict, with the cap in place. **Read.** The author's claim that \"a review report is some tens of kilobytes at most\" is also unmeasured.\n- **terminal-clean: hunk matching changes.** `plain()` now runs on parsed file names, and `locationKey` (`loader.ts`) and `carry.ts` (`h.file === stored.file`) compare them. Existing notes whose file names contain control bytes will stop matching and show as missing. **Read.** Low likelihood.\n- **sync-tracking: partial guard.** The check only requires the fetched ref to be a commit. A remote can still publish a commit with a non-notes tree, and that is adopted. Not tested. **Read.**\n- **Confirmed open risk (in TODO, correctly flagged):** the refspec-glob fetch break is verified above; a remote can make `git fetch` fail for every user until they run `git remote prune`.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
