 lean, and the five below are small tidy-ups.\n\n1. **`src/reviews.ts` (group `review-cap`, ~line 105): split the lines once.**\n   - `readReviews` filters `all` twice, once to count long lines and once to drop them. The warning key `${sha}:${long}` is also awkward.\n   - Instead, partition into `kept` and `long` in one pass, and key `warnedLong` on `sha` alone.\n   - The `isDecisionLine` exemption in the count is harmless but easy to misread, because the next filter drops those lines too.\n   - Effort: about 6 lines. **Read.**\n\n2. **`src/reviews.ts:6-8` (group `terminal-clean`): drop the `export { plain }` re-export.**\n   - `plain` now lives in `plain.ts`, but `src/commands/show.ts:9` and `src/commands/reviews.ts:5` still import it from `reviews.ts`.\n   - Those two imports should point at `./plain.ts`. Then `reviews.ts` needs no `plain` import or re-export, and the dependency is direct.\n   - Effort: 3 lines. **Read** (I grepped the importers).\n\n3. **`src/commands/sync.ts` (group `sync-tracking`, h5 and h6): fold fetch and check into one helper.**\n   - Both call sites write `git(['fetch', '-q', remote, `+${ref}:${tracking}`]); checkTracking(...)`.\n   - A single `fetchTracking(remote, ref, tracking)` would stop the next third fetch site from forgetting the check.\n   - Effort: about 5 lines. **Read.**\n\n4. **`src/loader.ts` (group `note-limits`, h21): flatten the claim count.**\n   - The nested `reduce` plus a `sizes` map is hard to read.\n   - Clearer: `const size = (h) => changedCount(h)`, then `for (const g of groups) for (const h of g.hunks) if (h.current) claimed += h.lines?.size ?? size(h.current)`, and `total` as a sum over `current`.\n   - Same behaviour, and no `!` assertion.\n   - Effort: about 6 lines. **Read.**\n\n5. **`src/html/client.js` (group `markdown-bound`, h17): the link regex limits the same thing twice.**\n   - The `{1,200}` and `{1,400}` quantifiers sit on top of the `slice(i, i + MAX_SPAN)`.\n   - Slicing to `MAX_SPAN` already bounds