 loop gives the same result with one bound to read. Size: 3 lines in the client file. Equivalence is by reasoning only; the `quadratic` test in `test/untrusted.test.ts` would confirm it if run.\n\n3. **`terminal-clean`, `src/commands/review.ts` line 24 and `src/render.ts` line 112.** The `old → new` file label is built in two places, and both now wrap it in `plain()`. A `fileLabel(h: Hunk)` helper in `render.ts`, returning `plain(...)`, used by `hunkLabel` and by `hunkLine` in `review.ts`, removes the duplicated expression and keeps the cleaning in one place. The change is about 5 lines, and the `hunkLine` and `hunkLabel` outputs are unchanged.\n\n4. **`sync-tracking`, `src/commands/sync.ts` lines 56–66.** `checkTracking` is called only from `fetchTracking`, so the two can be merged into one function with the `rev-parse` check after the fetch. That is one fewer helper and one fewer name to follow. Size: about 8 lines.\n\nThe rest is lean. The `Object.create(null)` maps and `Object.hasOwn` in `stage-lookup` are the smallest fix for each case, and a `Map` would not read better. The `warnedLong` Set follows the warn-once pattern already in `src/safe-match.ts`.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
