50d6` on the new one.\n- `git gloss show` on the old build prints `honesty: no issues`. On the new build it prints `honesty: gloss changed since review`.\n\nNothing in the gloss changed, but the honesty and improve reviews no longer count, so the commit looks unreviewed until someone reviews it again. `adopt` and `carry` also now write the cleaned text back, which permanently rewrites the stored note.\n\n**Possible fixes:**\n- Hash the raw annotation for stamps (have `stamp` read an uncleaned note) and clean only for display.\n- Or keep `\\r` when `multiline` is set.\n\n### Checked and found sound\n- The `ary` `new URL` crash fix.\n- The `sync` tracking-ref check.\n- The review-size caps, both on read and on `--record`.\n- The `Object.hasOwn` fix for stage names.\n- The prototype-free read sets in `client.js`.\n- The markdown span caps.\n\nOne thing I'm not counting as a new defect: a refused gloss (over the claim budget) now aborts `why` as well as `html`/`show`. A malformed note already did that, and TODO.md lists it as a follow-up.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
